    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 13.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>And lochwa þone flyman fede oððe feormie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.19"/>, gylde V pund þam cingce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.10-2"/>, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.20"/> he hine geladige, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine fleame nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ lóchwá ðone fleman féde oððe feormie, gylde fif pund ðam cýnge, butan he hine geladige, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine flema<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.2"/> nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>And lochwa þone flyman fede oððe feormige, gylde fif pund þam cyningce, buton he hine geladige, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine fleame nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui forsbannitum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.14"/> pauerit uel ei firmationem aliquam exhibuerit, emendet regi V libras<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.15"/>, nisi se adlegiet, quod infugatum eum nesciebat.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.16"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Et qui exulem (quem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.18"/> Angli uocant utlaga) pauerit post expulsionem, quod Angli dicunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.19-2"/> fede oþþe fermie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.20-2"/>, det regi centum solidos, nisi se purgauerit, quod illum nescisset expulsum clamatum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.1"/>, quod Angli dicunt gecydne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/> utlage.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Quicunque etiam illum exlegem pauerit uel procurauerit, soluat V libras regi, nisi iurauerit, quod illum exlegem esse nesciuit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="13.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="180" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ lóchwá ðone fleman féde oððe feormie, gylde fif pund ðam cýnge, butan he hine geladige þæt he hine flema nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="260" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And lochwa þone flyman fede oððe feormie, gylde V pund þam cingce, butan he hine geladige, þæt he hine fleame nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wer immer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.de.1"/> jenen Geächteten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.de.2"/> nährt oder herbergt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.de.3"/>, zahle dem König 5<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.de.4"/> Pfund, es sei denn, er erweise sich rein, dass er ihn nicht in Verbannung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_13-2.lnote.de.5"/> gewusst habe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever feeds or harbours that outlaw, let him pay the king 5 pounds, unless he clears himself [by showing] that he did not know him to be outlawed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_13-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="181" ed="#robertson"/>And whoever feeds or harbours the fugitive shall pay £5<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_13-2.robnote.n.2"/> to the king, unless he clear himself by a declaration that he did not know<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_13-2.robnote.n.3"/> that he was a fugitive.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="463" ed="#whitelock"/>And whoever feeds or harbours the fugitive is to pay five pounds to the king, unless he clear himself, that he did not know him to be a fugitive.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="261" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And anyone who feeds or shelters a fugitive must pay five pounds to the king, unless he can exonerate himself by proving that he did not know he was a fugitive.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="317"><ref target="clause:IIAs_20-8">II As 20.8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 20, 8</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_20-8">II As 20.8</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 13:2: (II As 20:8)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">B's ‘flema’ (as ‘outlaw’) — Liebermann suggests B may mean the instrumental of ‘fle(a)m’ (outlawry). Liebermann compares II As 20.8.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 317, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e. i. <hi rend="italic">aus Hk; fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e. i. from Hk; lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eum <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eum Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fleman <hi rend="italic">‘als Geächteten’ nach II As.</hi> 20, 8 <hi rend="italic">verstehen Frühere; doch meint vielleicht auch B den Instrumentalis von</hi> fle(a)m <hi rend="italic">‘Ächtung’; vgl.</hi> freoma 16</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Earlier editors take fleman as ‘as an outlaw’, following II As. 20, 8; but perhaps B too means the instrumental of fle(a)m ‘outlawry’; cf. freoma 16</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forisb. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forisb. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so KT;</hi> libris <hi rend="italic">DmR</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus KT; libris DmR</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">statt</hi> 14 <hi rend="italic">s. oben Anm.</hi>**</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for 14 see note ** above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-mige, g. fif p. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-mige, g. fif p. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyning <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyning Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q. A. u. u. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q. A. u. u. lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.19-2" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uocant <hi rend="italic">LbS; am Rande</hi> <hi rend="spaced">flemeneferme</hi> <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uocant LbS; in the margin <hi rend="italic">flemeneferme</hi> S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oðe forðie <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> en ferme <hi rend="italic">LbS</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oðe forðie Cb; en ferme LbS</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">damnatum <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">damnatum S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gekidne <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> cuth <hi rend="italic">LbS</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gekidne H; cuth LbS</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ga <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> -ave <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ga H; -ave S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘man beachte’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. lochwær u</hi>. 80, 1; <hi rend="italic">lochwilc</hi> Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Dipl</hi>. 391; Toller s. v. <hi rend="italic">loc</hi>; Kluge in <hi rend="italic">Beitr. Gsch. Dt. Spra</hi>. VIII 530</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘let it be noted’; <hi rend="italic">cf. lochwær below</hi> 80, 1; <hi rend="italic">lochwilc</hi> Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Dipl</hi>. 391; Toller s. v. <hi rend="italic">loc</hi>; Kluge in <hi rend="italic">Beitr. Gsch. Dt. Spra</hi>. VIII 530</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> friedlos 1b. h (<hi rend="italic">utlaga</hi> ist Nord. Lehnwort fürs Agsä. <hi rend="italic">fliema</hi>); Begünstigung 5. 14; Gefährdeeid 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> friedlos 1b. h (<hi rend="italic">utlaga</hi> is a Norse loan-word for the Anglo-Saxon <hi rend="italic">fliema</hi>); Begünstigung 5. 14; Gefährdeeid 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Wb: firma, -re, -tio</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Wb: firma, -re, -tio</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Strenger <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 66, 1.—Die 100 Schill. für 5 £ in In sind wie <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 30, 2¹ Normannische; es ist ‘Königsschutz’-Busse; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5. 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">More severe <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 66, 1.—The 100 shill. for £5 in In are, as <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 30, 2¹, Norman shillings; it is the compensation for the ‘king's protection’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5. 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_13-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hinzuzudenken ist <hi rend="italic">gangendne</hi>, das in Agsä. Syntax fortbleiben darf; solch Instrumental auch Toller 291b. l. 7. Die Lateiner verstehen Acc., wie II As 20, 8.—Über <hi rend="italic">gecyd utlah</hi> in Inst <hi rend="italic">s. Wb: cyðan</hi>. Die Agsä. Ann. a. 1014. 1052 haben <hi rend="italic">utlage(de) (ge)cweðan</hi> technisch neben <hi rend="italic">(ge)utlagian</hi> ‘ächten’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">gangendne</hi> is to be understood, which may be omitted in Anglo-Saxon syntax; for such an instrumental see also Toller 291b. l. 7. The Latin translators take it as an acc., as in II As 20, 8.—On <hi rend="italic">gecyd utlah</hi> in Inst <hi rend="italic">see Wb: cyðan</hi>. The A.-S. Ann. a. 1014. 1052 have <hi rend="italic">utlage(de) (ge)cweðan</hi> as a technical term alongside <hi rend="italic">(ge)utlagian</hi> ‘to outlaw’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_13-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 20, 8.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_13-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. cap. 66, 1, where the penalty is much more severe.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_13-2.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 20, 8, where, however, the MSS have <hi rend="italic">flyman</hi> (<hi rend="italic">flymene</hi>, Ld). I do not understand the forms <hi rend="italic">flema</hi>, <hi rend="italic">fleame</hi>. Toller, <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> p. 224, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi> <hi rend="italic">fleam</hi>, apparently takes the latter as a form (? dative) of <hi rend="italic">fleam</hi>, but is not <hi rend="italic">on</hi> required in that case? Liebermann suggests that the word <hi rend="italic">gangende</hi> is understood and that the form <hi rend="italic">fleame</hi> is instrumental.</seg></note>
      </div>
